  "answer": "### Short Answer\n\n### Interpretation\nThis section outlines the deadlines for filing income tax returns for individuals, establishing April 15 as the annual due date. It also includes specific provisions for individuals subject to capital gains tax, requiring them to file returns within thirty (30) days after each transaction involving the sale or exchange of shares or real property.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nTaxpayers must ensure that their income tax returns are submitted by the April 15 deadline to avoid penalties and interest. This provision emphasizes the importance of timely filing and compliance with tax obligations, particularly for those engaged in transactions that may trigger additional filing requirements.",
